atches from the real matching module, and where a value genuinely does not exist the UI renders an explicit placeholder rather than inventing one. I will NOT hardcode 92 percent or a company called Infosys. If you want the screenshot's literal strings rendered as a visual mock, say so explicitly and I will scope it as a static mock instead - but I will not silently fabricate. FOURTH, MY RECON ESTABLISHED WHAT IS NEW VERSUS WHAT EXISTS, AND THIS DRIVES THE ORDER: the bottom three-column analytics DO NOT EXIST anywhere in src - a repo-wide sweep found Application Progress, Top Job Matches and Your Next Steps only in DashboardSettings and the marketing pricing page - and there is NO chart component in the codebase (only Form/progress-bar and marketing HomepageSteps). There is also NO Upgrade to Pro card in CubaAppShell. By contrast the header surface, the toolbar category pills, the resume card action row from DIR-086, and the rail's AiCareerBriefing plus Quick-Pitch ALL already exist. So areas 5 and 7 are greenfield builds and areas 1 through 4 and 6 are refinements. THE RECOMMENDED SEAM: DIR-092a would cover areas 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 7 - header, metric card polish, toolbar with Ctrl+K sort and Grid/List toggle, resume cards with badges and the dashed create card, the rail copilot, and the sidebar promo. That is all layout and wiring over data sources that ALREADY EXIST, so it is achievable completely in one pass. DIR-092b would cover area 5, the bottom analytics, which is the only genuinely new subsystem - it needs a real grouped bar chart built with no charting dependency, a real job-match list, and a next-steps checklist derived from real profile completeness, each needing its own data-lineage verification. I will execute in that order regardless: refinements first, analytics last, so that if budget runs out the delivered surface is coherent rather than half-built. INVARIANTS I WILL HOLD: sub-4s Vite build, 0 lint errors, frozen 55 CV templates at diff 0, XAMPP-only servers, zero synthetic data, no auth or API or DB or RBAC change, and tests/dir092-candidate-dashboard-reference-layout.test.mjs passing 100 percent. I will also re-declare any supersession explicitly rather than quietly breaking an earlier directive's pins, exactly as I did for DIR-085 under DIR-091."
